                <pb facs="0882" n="756" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg756"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/6319: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Canton</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jenkins</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-07-01T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 1, 1925—6
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your June 26, 11 a.m. You should tactfully decline to sit on proposed commission
                    of inquiry unless officially requested to do so by the British and French
                    Consuls General and unless common foreign interests would be furthered by your
                    participation in which case you should telegraph your views stating also the
                    composition and defined objects of the commission and await further
                    instructions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
